# RemoEdPH Stable Surfaces

Before changing shared auth, booking, class schedule, or Mongo scripts, read [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md). Prefer **new routes and thin wrappers** beside these paths; do not “simplify” them.

## Live data / Mongo

- Production DB is Atlas **`test`**. Keep `MONGODB_URI` ending in `/test`. Do not drop or rename `test` unless the user explicitly requests a launch wipe.
- Do not delete GridFS `presentations/` or `portal-videos/` to free space. Classroom recordings under `classroom-recordings/` were intentionally purged.
- Archive/purge scripts may only target legacy DB / recordings; never change `KEEP` counts for `students`, `teachers`, `admins`, `lessons`, `curriculums`:
  - `scripts/archive-legacy-mongo-db.js`
  - `scripts/purge-beta-recordings.js`
- Atlas M0 storage meter staying high after deletes is expected (no `compact`).

## Portal auth tokens

- Client keys: `remoed_admin_token` / `remoed_teacher_token` / `remoed_student_token` (`public/js/user-session.js`, `public/js/remoed-auth-token.js`).
- `server/authMiddleware.js` enforces portal separation (`WRONG_PORTAL_TOKEN`). Student JWT may call only the teacher-route allowlist (`/api/teacher/slots`, paths ending `/book-class`, `/available-teachers`, `/public/...`). **Extend** the allowlist for new student needs; do not remove the gate.
- `GET /api/teacher/slots` and public profile routes are intentionally usable without Bearer. Do not lock them behind teacher auth without a student replacement.

## Student booking

- Preferred client: `POST /api/student/book-class` (`public/student-book.html`).
- Handler chain: `server/student.js` → `server/studentController.js` → `server/services/studentBookSlotService.js`. Keep `POST /api/teacher/book-class` equivalent (same handler).
- **Never** declare `require('./studentController')` twice in `server/student.js` (caused production 502).
- Resolve teacher identity with `resolveToCanonicalTeacherId` / `findOpenTeacherSlotByUtcAndNormalizedTeacher` (`server/services/teacherSlotResolve.js`). UI may send email via `teacherBookingKey` (`server/teacher.js`) while slots store username — do not require email-only preferred IDs.
- Persist `Booking.teacherId` as canonical `Teacher.teacherId`. `Booking.studentId` is student **username**, not Mongo `_id`. Prefer `/api/student/bookings*`.
- Book body must include Mongo `slotId`. Schedule matching uses UTC `dateTimeUtc` (±2s).
- Credits: available = `creditBalance` only (`server/services/studentCreditSummary.js`). Expiry via `server/services/creditExpiry.js`. Product codes `SUBSCRIPTION_REQUIRED_LESSON_2`, `CREDITS_EXPIRED`, `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`, `TRIAL_LESSON_1_ONLY` are expected gates, not route bugs. Do not reverse already-booked classes on expiry.

## Teacher Class Schedule / Report Issue

- `public/teacher-class-table.html`: keep **one** live `resolveTeacherPortalToken` in the main schedule `<script>` (and on `window`). Do not “fix” only the weaker head-script duplicate. Use that helper for Bearer calls — not bare `localStorage.getItem('token')`.
- Issue modal needs `window.__reportIssueBooking` / `closeClassInfo({ keepBooking: true })`. Do not wrap the main script in an IIFE/`type="module"` without exporting `onclick` handlers.
- `POST /api/teacher/report-issue` ownership must use canonical teacher IDs. If you touch it, also align `GET /check-class-issues` (must not stay on raw string equality alone).

## Applicant documents

- On teacher invite signup, `server/utils/applicantDocuments.js` copies application ID/NBI onto teacher profile. Keep that on create; do not strip URL-style `fileData` when saving teacher documents.

## Live classroom (Settings, locks, VBG)

Do not rewrite `public/live-classroom.html` socket/settings/VBG unless the user asks. Details: [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md) § Live classroom.

- Teacher Settings is `#lc-class-settings-overlay` (body-level). Do not move the panel back into `.tabs` / `.center-panel`.
- Room settings: `classroomSettingsByRoom` `{ videosAllowed, penAllowed }`. Queue early `classroom-settings` on `pendingClassroomSettingsBySocket`; flush on `join` / `join-room`. Students use `classroom-settings-request`. **Do not** delete room settings when the last socket leaves. **Do not** re-broadcast default `true` after teacher join (unlocks students).
- Videos lock hides student `#lc-videos-tab-btn`. Pen lock is `window.__lcStudentPenAllowed` (lesson + board). `whiteboard-mode-stop` still sends students to Lesson.
- Student mic/cam: `media-control` (`true` = allowed). Rail pills `#lc-teacher-media-controls` are text chips, **not** `.video-control-btn`. Highlight **both** sides of each pair (`syncTeacherMediaUi`).
- VBG: `public/js/virtual-background.js` canvas-first; presets `public/images/virtual-bg/{office,classroom,nature}.jpg`. Do not switch presets back to `.svg`. Do not let `applyTeacherCameraReadyLook()` overwrite an active VBG.

## Responsive / overlays

Details: [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md) § Phone app shell.

- Tokens: [public/css/remoed-layers.css](public/css/remoed-layers.css). Breakpoints 768 / 1024 only for new portal CSS. Phone `.remoed-content` margin is 0 — do not reintroduce `margin-left: 260px` without a `max-width: 768` override.
- Phone app chrome: hide `nav.remoed-sidebar`; titled top bar + 4 tabs + More sheet on `document.body` (`public/js/portal-layout.js`). Do not add a hamburger drawer or a second teacher drawer at 992 (`z-index: 9999`). Classroom keeps `#lc-mobile-dock` (Lesson / Camera / Chat).
- **Adopt `.nav-right` only at ≤768.** On ≥769, `releaseHeaderActions()` so Time In / bell / calendar stay in `.nav-header` (the mobile shell is `display: none` on desktop).
- Phone scroll: lock `html`/`body`; **`.remoed-main` is the only scroller** (`height: 100%`, `box-sizing: border-box`, `overflow-y: auto`). Do not set `.remoed-main { height: auto }`. Do not add `window.scrollTo(0,0)` on scroll, lastY snap guards, or `PullToRefresh` on `.remoed-content`.
- Modals use `--z-modal` / `--z-toast` / `--z-blocking` on `document.body`. Do not raise raw z-index or put popovers inside `overflow: hidden` / `backdrop-filter` parents.

## Landing culture / gender

Details: [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md) § Landing culture / about and § Gender.

- Homepage culture blocks after hero stay in order Who we are → Principles → Pillars → HEART → Vision/Mission. Pillars/HEART use **icons**, not cropped culture photos.
- Profile gender selects: **Male / Female only**. Do not restore Other. Teacher enum and profile saves must reject/clear Other.

## Admin Marketing Hub

Details: [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md) § Admin Marketing Hub and § Admin Roles and Access.

- Sidebar order: **Accounting Hub** → **Admin Fee** → **Marketing Hub**. Marketing Hub owns Unique Link Commissions. Do not put commissions back as an Accounting Hub tab.
- Accounting Hub tabs: Payroll Management, **Admin Payroll** (dispense admin fees), Student Subscriptions.
- `admin-unique-link-commission.html` standalone → `admin-marketing-hub.html`.
- Role access is **dynamic RBAC** (Settings → Admin Roles and Access). Default seed for `admin_marketing` matches the former whitelist (no Settings / System monitor). Extend via permission keys in `server/services/adminRbac.js`, not hardcoded sidebar branches alone.
- Keep `adminRoleGate` / `requirePermission` / `admin-access-guard.js` in sync when adding admin pages.

## Teaching Fee bonus / incentive

Details: [docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md](docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md) § Teaching Fee — Bonus / Incentive.

- Keep **Bonus / Incentive** under Period fee on Teaching Fee (read-only for teachers). Accounting edits it on Payroll per cut-off; include in net pay / dispense / payslip. Do not make it a fixed monthly entitlement.

## Before push

- Run `node --check` on edited server entry files (`server/student.js`, `server/index.js`, etc.).
- After production deploy, re-run the smoke checklist in `docs/STABLE_BASELINE.md`.
